  "feedbacks": [],
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 15 actions (actions.js, returned by compileActionDefinitions) and no feedbacks (index.js never calls setFeedbackDefinitions). Variables and presets do not exist in the source either (the module is a single index.js plus actions.js).",
    "Protocol: AMCP over TCP (TCPHelper) to the configured host and port (config: host with Regex.IP, port default 5250 with Regex.PORT; index.js getConfigFields). Commands are sent with a trailing CRLF. On connect the module sends CLS and TLS to fill the clip and template dropdowns.",
    "Almost every field is a text input, so channel and layer values are strings; the source default for channel is the number 1 (recorded as written). Layer may be empty (the command then addresses the whole channel). The regex values are the resolved constants: Regex.NUMBER is /^\\d+$/ in @companion-module/base 1.4.3 (dist/module-api/enums.js).",
    "LOADBG/LOAD/PLAY share one option list: clip_dd (dropdown from CLS) and the free-text \"clip\" are alternatives, the text field wins when both are set. A transition other than CUT appends the transition, parseFloat(duration) and the tween (an empty duration yields NaN).",
    "Source quirk, kept as written: the transition dropdown lists WIPE with id \"CUT\" (actions.js:99), so choosing WIPE sends no transition. The catalog therefore contains the id \"CUT\" twice (labels CUT and WIPE); the first entry is the default.",
    "Source quirk: SWAP builds a command starting with NaN (see the action description), so it does not send a valid AMCP SWAP command.",
    "Source quirk: CG ADD sends the template-data argument only when \"variables\" is not empty (as \"<flag> \\\"<xml or json>\\\"\"); build_templatedata_string returns null when no key=\"value\" pair parses, and the callback then throws on templ.replace.",
    "Variable expansion: only COMMAND (cmd) and GOTO (offset) declare useVariables, but sendCommand runs parseVariablesInString over the complete command text, so a $(...) in any text field is expanded by the module (actions.js:140).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.3: option values cannot be expressions."
  ]
}
